  "worked_solution": "We have the following number lines:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191664/assets/2334f6ee136334c70b658c41a6bc0ec578b135c7c6bc9ef87a0f8d156a7db01c.png)\n\nThe union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191664/assets/32899816340ae23edc2fdca86e13a1d04e04af1e5723beda1a684c6e51e16f4d.png)\n\nThe corresponding inequality is $x\\le 1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
