  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-44866\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>We have the following number lines:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-44866\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-44866\"></div>\n\n<p>The union of the two intervals consists of all the points which are contained within at least one of the intervals. So, to graph the union of the two intervals, we take the graphs of the individual intervals and lay them on top of each other.</p>\n<p>The resulting graph is as follows:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-44866-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-44866-e-1\"></div>\n\n<p>The corresponding inequality is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"25\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2264\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</div>",
